Build succeeds with no errors. Here's a summary of the changes:

**The fix:** In MSTest v4, `TestMethodAttribute` no longer has a parameterless constructor — it requires an explicit `string? displayName` parameter. Add `: base(null)` to your derived constructor:

```csharp
public CategorizedTestMethodAttribute(string category)
    : base(null)  // ← required in MSTest v4
{
    Category = category;
}
```

Also, `[TestMethod("display name")]` (positional string) is deprecated in v4. Use the named property instead: `[TestMethod(DisplayName = "My custom display name")]`.
